        "original_id": "3ef8b0ac-48a2-5a16-8e79-f6fcb0cc4224",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Super Furry Animals, Social Distortion\n- People: Gruff Rhys, Huw Bunford, Guto Pryce, Cian Ciaran, Dafydd Ieuan, Mike Ness, Jonny Wickersham, Brent Harding, David Hidalgo Jr., David Kalish\n- Music releases: \"Bing Bong\"\n- Places: Cardiff, Wales, Bing Bong, Borroloola, King Ash Bay\n- Infrastructure: Carpentaria Highway, McArthur River mineral deposits, port facilities\n\nFacts:\n- Super Furry Animals formed in Cardiff, Wales in 1993.\n- Since 1993, Super Furry Animals has consisted of Gruff Rhys on lead vocals and guitar, Huw Bunford on lead guitar and vocals, Guto Pryce on bass guitar, Cian Ciaran on keyboards, synthesisers, electronics, occasional guitar, and vocals, and Dafydd Ieuan on drums and vocals.\n- Social Distortion currently consists of Mike Ness on lead vocals and lead guitar, Jonny Wickersham on rhythm guitar and backing vocals, Brent Harding on bass and backing vocals, David Hidalgo Jr. on drums, and David Kalish on keyboards.\n- The Super Furry Animals single \"Bing Bong\" was released on 13 May 2016.\n- The Carpentaria Highway provides road access to the McArthur River mineral deposits, the port facilities at Bing Bong, the community of Borroloola, and King Ash Bay.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
